.TH PATHMUX 1 "February 2026" "v0.8.99b" "PathMux Dashcam Explorer Manual"
.SH NAME
pathmux \- Trip manager and video builder for Pruveeo D90 four-channel dashcam footage
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pathmux
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIPATH\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pathmux
scans storage containing footage from a Pruveeo D90 360\[de] four-channel dashcam
(Front, Rear, Left, Right cameras), groups video segments into trips based on
timestamp gaps, and caches the results as JSON manifests.  Trips can be browsed
interactively, exported as GPX or KML tracks, and assembled into per-camera MP4
files or a synchronized 4K collage.
.PP
Dashcam footage is stored as MPEG-TS segments named
.IR YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS_X.ts .
The Front camera is the primary anchor for trip detection; the other cameras are
fuzzy-matched within a configurable time window.  All timestamp comparisons use
Unix epoch arithmetic to handle midnight and year boundaries correctly.
.PP
Manifests are cached in
.IR ~/.config/pathmux/ .
Each cached path is assigned a two-character alphanumeric manifest ID from an
unambiguous character set (ambiguous pairs such as O/0 and I/1 are collapsed).
IDs are reused when manifests are deleted, keeping the list compact.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS "Scan & Display"
.TP
.BI \-s " PATH" ", " \-\-scan " PATH"
Scan
.I PATH
for dashcam footage and build a trip manifest.  Always re-scans even if a
cached manifest exists.
.TP
.BI \-p " PATH" ", " \-\-path " PATH"
Set the active path.  Uses the cached manifest if one exists; scans if not.
.TP
.B \-t ", " \-\-trips
Show a one-line summary for every trip in the active manifest (default).
.TP
.B \-T ", " \-\-alltrips
Show a full segment tree for every trip (Front/Rear/Left/Right per segment).
.TP
.B \-l ", " \-\-list
List all cached manifests with their assigned IDs and paths.
.TP
.B \-I ", " \-\-manifests
Interactive manifest browser.  Select a manifest then browse its trips.
Pressing
.B B
returns to the manifest list.
.TP
.B \-i ", " \-\-inter
Interactive trip browser for the last-used manifest.
.TP
.B \-R ", " \-\-refresh
Re-scan and refresh the last-used manifest.
.SS "GPS & Export"
.TP
.B \-g ", " \-\-gps
Extract GPS data from footage into the manifest (no file output).
Requires ExifTool 13.51 or later.
.TP
.B \-G ", " \-\-gpx
Extract GPS if needed and write a GPX track file.
.TP
.BI \-\-gpxpath " DIR"
Output directory for GPX files (default: current directory).
.TP
.BI \-\-gpxfile " NAME"
Explicit GPX filename.  Use
.B all
to write one file per trip with
.I .1 .2
suffixes to avoid overwrites.
.TP
.B \-K ", " \-\-kml
Extract GPS if needed and write a KML track file.
.TP
.BI \-\-kmlpath " DIR"
Output directory for KML files (default: current directory).
.TP
.BI \-\-kmlfile " NAME"
Explicit KML filename.  Use
.B all
to write one file per trip with
.I .1 .2
suffixes to avoid overwrites.
.TP
.B \-\-force
Overwrite existing export files without prompting.
.PP
Default output filenames are derived from the first segment timestamp:
.IR 20260216_095422.gpx " / " 20260216_095422.kml .
.SS "Video Build"
.TP
.B \-V ", " \-\-video
Launch the interactive video build menu.  Loads the last-used manifest,
displays trips, and prompts for build options.  Press
.B M
to switch to a different manifest.
.PP
The following flags may be combined with
.B \-V
to pre-set options or run non-interactively.  When
.B \-\-trip
is supplied the menu is skipped entirely.
.TP
.BI \-\-manifest " ID"
Select manifest by two-character ID (case-insensitive).  Required for
non-interactive use.
.TP
.BI \-\-trip " N"
Select trip
.I N
(1-based) within the chosen manifest.  Required for non-interactive use.
.TP
.B \-\-build-front=yes|no
Include the Front camera file in output (default: yes).
.TP
.B \-\-build-rear=yes|no
Include the Rear camera file in output (default: yes).
.TP
.B \-\-build-left=yes|no
Include the Left camera file in output (default: yes).
.TP
.B \-\-build-right=yes|no
Include the Right camera file in output (default: yes).
.TP
.B \-\-build-collage4k=yes|no
Build a 3840x2160 H.265 collage (default: yes).
.TP
.B \-\-build-collage1080p=yes|no
Transcode the 4K collage to 1920x1080 H.264 (default: no).
Always derived from the 4K master; never assembled from source again.
.TP
.BI \-\-output-format " FMT"
Container format for per-camera files:
.BR mp4 ", " mkv ", " mov ", " avi ", " mpg
(default: mp4).  Collage files are always MP4.
.TP
.BI \-\-output-path " DIR"
Write output files to
.IR DIR .
Overrides the default export directory from preferences.
.TP
.BI \-\-on-conflict " ACTION"
Action when
.B \-\-man-id
conflicts with an existing manifest:
.BR append ", " overwrite ", " fail
(default when non-interactive: fail).
.SS "Settings"
.TP
.B \-P ", " \-\-prefs
Launch the interactive preferences editor.  Settings are saved to
.IR ~/.config/pathmux/pathmux.json .
.TP
.B \-\-kmlprefs
Launch the interactive KML visual preferences editor (track colors, line
width, pin icons, known location overlay).
.TP
.B \-\-locations
Manage known locations (Home, Work, etc.) used for KML proximity pins.
.TP
.BI \-\-set " key=value"
Set a preference non-interactively.  Currently supported keys:
.RS
.TP
.B gap=\fIN\fR
Trip gap threshold in seconds.
.RE
.TP
.BI \-\-man-id " XX"
Assign a specific two-character manifest ID when scanning a new path.
If the ID is already in use, behaviour depends on
.BR \-\-on-conflict .
Interactive sessions prompt the user; non-interactive sessions fail by default.
.TP
.B \-\-clear-cache
Remove all cached manifests.  Settings and known locations are preserved.
.TP
.B \-v ", " \-\-version
Print version and exit.
.TP
.B \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a usage summary and exit.
.SH "VIDEO BUILD PIPELINE"
Per-camera files use ffmpeg concat demuxer with stream copy
.RB ( "\-c copy" ).
Only the video and audio streams are mapped
.RB ( "\-map 0:v:0 \-map 0:a:0" );
the LIGOGPSINFO data track embedded in the MPEG-TS container is discarded.
GPS data is already in the manifest at this point and does not need to travel
with the video file.
.PP
The 4K collage is assembled as follows:
.IP 1. 4
Per segment, ffprobe measures the frame count of all four cameras.
.IP 2. 4
Cameras shorter than the longest are padded with a fade-to-black tail
.RB ( tpad " + " fade " filters) and silent audio (" apad ).
This prevents sync drift from accumulating across a long trip.
.IP 3. 4
The four normalized streams are combined with the
.B xstack
filter into a 3840x2160 frame (Front/Rear top row, Left/Right bottom row).
.IP 4. 4
Audio is taken exclusively from the Left camera
.RB ( "\-map 2:a:0" ),
which records the driver position and provides lip-sync reference.
.IP 5. 4
Output is encoded as H.265
.RB ( "libx265 \-crf 18 \-preset slow" )
— visually lossless at roughly half the file size of equivalent H.264.
.PP
The optional 1080p collage is a simple transcode of the finished 4K master
.RB ( "scale=1920:1080" ", " "libx264 \-crf 20 \-preset fast" )
with the audio stream copied without re-encoding.
.SH "GPS EXTRACTION"
GPS extraction requires ExifTool 13.51 or later.  The EPEL package (13.10)
does
.B not
work — it cannot correctly decode the LIGOGPSINFO binary stream embedded in
Pruveeo D90 footage.  Phil Harvey fixed the coordinate decode issue in 13.51
following a bug report.
.PP
One GPS fix per second is available.  The extractor scans from t=0 of the
first segment and uses the first fix with a non-zero latitude and longitude,
avoiding the cold-start window without wasting a fixed offset on trips where
the GPS receiver achieves a hot start immediately.  The cold-start fallback
is 45 seconds if no valid fix is found earlier.
.PP
Altitude values from the D90 are systematically incorrect (negative) and are
ignored.  Speed is recorded in km/h; the dashcam OSD converts to mph for
display but the raw stream is metric.
.SS "ExifTool Options Preference"
The complete exiftool command line (excluding the binary path and the input
filename) is stored in the
.B exiftoolOptions
preference, editable via
.B \-\-prefs
option
.BR [O] .
The default value for Pruveeo D90 footage is:
.PP
.RS
.B \-ee3 \-p '$GPSDateTime $GPSLatitude# $GPSLongitude# $GPSSpeed# $GPSTrack#'
.RE
.PP
This string is passed verbatim between the binary path and the quoted filename.
The assembled command is:
.PP
.RS
.RI exiftool " OPTIONS" " \(dqfile.ts\(dq"
.RE
.PP
.B Important constraints when modifying this value:
.TP
.B Field order is fixed.
The output parser expects exactly five space-separated tokens per line after
the date and time:
.IR latitude ,
.IR longitude ,
.IR speed ,
.IR heading .
Do not reorder, add, or remove fields from the
.B \-p
format string without corresponding changes to the parser source.
.TP
.B The \-p flag and format string must be included.
Unlike most tool preferences which store only extraction flags,
.B exiftoolOptions
must contain the complete options string including
.BR \-p .
This design allows the
.B \-p
flag itself to be omitted entirely for cameras that require a different
extraction approach (e.g.\&
.BR \-json ).
.TP
.B Single quotes are required around the format string.
The
.B \-p
argument must be quoted because it contains spaces and
.B $
characters.
Single quotes prevent the shell from expanding
.B $GPSDateTime
etc. as variables.
Double quotes would also expand
.BR $GPSTrack ,
corrupting the command.
When editing in the preferences menu, enter the value exactly as it would
appear on a shell command line.
.TP
.B The \-ee3 flag controls embedded stream extraction depth.
Level 3 is required for MPEG-TS files from the D90 because the GPS data
is in a private binary stream (LIGOGPSINFO) several levels deep in the
container.  Level 1
.RB ( \-ee )
and level 2
.RB ( \-ee2 )
do not reach it.
Other camera formats may work at lower levels or may not need
.B \-ee
at all.
.TP
.B The \-# numeric suffix on coordinate tags requests decimal degrees.
.B $GPSLatitude#
and
.B $GPSLongitude#
output signed decimal values (e.g.\&
.IR \-89.025 )
rather than the default DMS notation
.RI ( "89 deg 1' 30\(dq W" ).
The parser requires decimal form; remove the
.B #
suffix only if replacing the parser entirely.
.SH "MANIFEST IDS"
Manifests are assigned two-character IDs from an unambiguous alphanumeric
character set.  The following characters are excluded to avoid visual
confusion:
.PP
.RS
.B O
(same as
.BR 0 ),
.B I
and
.B L
(same as
.BR 1 ),
.B S
(same as
.BR 5 ),
.B Z
(same as
.BR 2 )
.RE
.PP
IDs are always displayed in upper case.  Input is case-insensitive.
The preferred sequence assigns a letter first character and digit second
character (A3, A4 ... Y9) giving 132 slots before spilling into
letter+letter combinations.  Deleted manifest IDs are returned to the pool
and reused from the lowest available position.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/pathmux/pathmux.json
Application settings and manifest ID table.
.TP
.I ~/.config/pathmux/<sanitized_path>.json
Cached trip manifest for a scanned path.  The path is sanitized by stripping
the leading
.B /
and replacing remaining
.B /
characters with
.BR _ .
.TP
.I ~/.config/pathmux/locations.json
Named locations (Home, Work, etc.) used for KML proximity pin overlays.
.TP
.I ~/.config/pathmux/<sanitized_path>.XX.bak
Backup of an overwritten manifest, where
.I XX
is the manifest ID.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Failure (bad arguments, missing path, manifest ID conflict in non-interactive
mode, or ffmpeg/ExifTool error).
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR ffmpeg (1),
.BR ffprobe (1),
.BR exiftool (1)
